# Retrieval artifacts are addressed by byte offset, or are raw binary, so Git
# must never rewrite their line endings.
#
# Measured failure: with core.autocrlf=true (the default for Git for Windows)
# `docs.cos.jsonl` was checked out as 10094 bytes instead of 10083 -- one extra
# byte per line -- while the binary `docs.cos.offsets.u64` was not converted.
# Every recorded offset then pointed one byte short of its row, and the reader
# failed with "Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)".
#
# `-text` stores and checks out the bytes verbatim on every platform.
*.jsonl -text
*.f32   -text -diff
*.sq8   -text -diff
*.int8  -text -diff
*.u64   -text -diff
*.faiss -text -diff
*.pkl   -text -diff
